{"id":"h264","run":2,"role":"test_wrong","category":"science-physics","question":"An airplane is flying at Mach 1.75 at an altitude of 8000 m, where the speed of sound is How long after the plane passes directly overhead will you hear the sonic boom? (Unit: m/s)\nIs the correct answer \"560\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"no","correct":false,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct answer is not 560.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1314},{"text":"The problem statement is incomplete because the speed of sound value is missing.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-0.0164},{"text":"The unit m/s is mismatched with a question asking for a time.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-0.0964},{"text":"The boom is heard when the Mach cone sweeps past the ground observer.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1376},{"text":"The time after the overhead pass is t = hM(1+1/M^2)/(a sqrt(M^2-1)), roughly 12,900/a seconds.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1413},{"text":"The speed of sound at 8000 m is roughly 310-340 m/s, giving a time of about 38-42 s.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1406},{"text":"Getting t = 560 s would require a speed of sound near 23 m/s, which is physically implausible.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1413},{"text":"The geometry and realistic speed of sound, not the unit, settle that 560 is wrong.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1317}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.3,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"suppor